# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend and build-time variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill it in.
#
# BACKEND variables do NOT belong here. Everything the Convex functions read
# lives on the deployment itself:
#
#   npx convex env set OPENROUTER_API_KEY sk-or-...
#
# The full list is in the README ("Environment variables").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Convex deployment the browser client connects to.
# `npx convex dev` writes this line for you on first run.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=

# --- Self-hosted Convex only -----------------------------------------------
# Where the CLI pushes functions, and the admin key printed by
# `docker compose exec backend ./generate_admin_key.sh`.
# Leave both empty when using Convex Cloud.
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY=

# --- Analytics (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Set these if you fork: src/lib/analytics.ts falls back to Nolënor's own
# PostHog project when they are empty, so a production build would send its
# telemetry there. Analytics are disabled in dev either way.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=

# --- Source maps (optional, build-time only) --------------------------------
# A personal PostHog API key enables source-map upload during `yarn build`,
# so production stack traces are readable. Without it the step is skipped.
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID=
# POSTHOG_HOST=
